instrument wingie
; grain — glass field: the Wingie's microphones as hi-fi grains.
; fader1 (Mix) density, fader2 (Decay) grain size, fader3 (Volume) where in the
; last 0.6 s the grains read. keys1 plays their pitch; hold mode1 to freeze the tape.
; The left LED follows the microphones, the right one the grains.

glass field
-----------
the field is grains 6 gauss
the hall is reverblite 2
mic.both -> field
keys1.pitch -> field.pitch
fader1 -> field.density
fader2 -> field.size
fader3 -> field.position
mode1 -> field.freeze
field -> left
field.right -> right
field field.right ~30> hall
hall -> out
mic.both -> lights.left
field -> lights.right

the photograph that breathes
----------------------------
; tap mode1 to hold the last moment as a drone; fader1 from the room to the
; held moment, fader2 how restless it is; keys1 sets a glisson choir above it
the photo is grainfreeze 6
the swallows are glisson 2
mic.both -> photo swallows
mode1.tap -> photo.capture
fader1 -> photo.blend
fader2 -> photo.drift
keys1.pitch -> swallows.glide
fader3 -> swallows.density
photo swallows -> left
photo.right swallows.right -> right
photo -> lights.left
swallows -> lights.right

the choir in the empty church
-----------------------------
; the microphones transposed onto a minor chord on keys1; fader1 density,
; fader2 size; fader3 how much of the cathedral of grains
the choir is harmonicgrains 3 minor
the sand is granularverb 3
mic.both -> choir
keys1.pitch -> choir.pitch
fader1 -> choir.density
fader2 -> choir.size
choir choir.right -> sand
fader3 -> sand.size
choir sand -> left
choir.right sand.right -> right
mic.both -> lights.left
sand -> lights.right
